[node name="PistolHoldPack" type="CbAnimPack"]
replaces = PackedStringArray("UpperBody")
character_name = "pistol.hold"
skeleton_path = NodePath("Skeleton3D")
animation_player_path = NodePath("AnimationPlayer")
animation_tree_path = NodePath("AnimationTree")
graph_inputs = {
"FullBody/Move/blend_position": "forward_speed"
}
editor_description = "How the pistol is held: an animation pack for the arms.

Its UpperBody state machine replaces a character's while a pistol is in the hand (pistol.cpp: ItemLayers). Hold is the idle; Shoot plays on the server's \"pistol.fired\" and returns when it ends.

The tree is the default one in full: FullBody (the locomotion), UpperBody over it, and UpperBodyBlend, which lays one over the other. Replaces is UpperBody: FullBody is here to see the arms over a walking body in the editor, and is not baked.

UpperBodyBlend's filter is the arms alone (shoulders to fingers). The spine, the neck and the head stay the character's own, so a body bends the same way to look up and down whatever it holds; only the arms are this item's.

The clips are in the AnimationPlayer node (animation_packs/source/*.res: the mannequin's, CC0; the placeholder's locomotion). Skeleton3D is the SDK's placeholder skeleton: leave it. Saving this scene bakes it into res://anim/pistol.hold/."

